-- title:
--   Unique descent of F[m]-invariant power series along [m]_F
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $F$ be an $n$-dimensional formal group law over $k$: a family $F_1,\dots,F_n$ of power series in the two blocks of variables $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}, X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$ with zero constant term, with $F_i$ having coefficient $\delta_{ij}$ at each of $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ and $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$, and satisfying the associativity identity in three blocks of variables; assume $F$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks fixes each $F_i$. Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$, and write $[m]_F$ for `F.nthSeries m`, defined by $[0]_F = 0$ and $[m+1]_F{}_i = F_i([m]_F(X), X)$. Assume the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of $[m]_F$ is a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space. Let $f \in k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ be such that, in the power series ring on the two blocks, $f(F(X,Y)) - f(X)$ lies in the ideal generated by the components of $[m]_F(Y)$, the substitution of the second block of variables into $[m]_F$. Then there is exactly one $G \in k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ with $f = G([m]_F(X))$.
--
--   This expresses that multiplication by $m$ on a commutative formal group law with finite kernel makes $F$ a torsor under $F[m]$: a formal function invariant under translation by the kernel is the pull-back along $[m]_F$ of a unique formal function, uniqueness coming from injectivity of substitution by $[m]_F$ and existence from descent along the finite flat substitution endomorphism. It feeds the construction of coboundaries for symmetric two-cocycles on $F$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_existsUnique_eq_subst_nthSeries_of_sub_mem_span.lean

